The message defined in Clause 8.2.26.1 is **TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT**, which is a **standard Layer 3 (L3) message** (per Clause [5]: *“every message, except the SERVICE REQUEST message, is a standard L3 message”*), and thus follows the structure defined in 3GPP TS 24.007 [12].

Its structure consists of:
- **Message type IE** (octet 1, mandatory, format T, value per Table 9.8.1/TS 24.301);
- **EPS bearer identity** (not present — only used in EPS Session Management messages; this is an EMM message);
- **Security header type** (octet 1 if security protected; otherwise absent in plain NAS);
- **Procedure transaction identity** (absent — only included in EPS Session Management messages per Clause [7] and [5]);
- **Other mandatory and conditional Information Elements (IEs)** as specified in Table 8.2.26.1, ordered with imperative (V, LV, LV-E) IEs before non-imperative (T, TV, TLV, TLV-E) IEs (Clause [1]b);
- If security protected: includes **message authentication code (MAC)** and encapsulates the plain NAS message (Clause [5]2).

Hence: **Standard L3 NAS message structure per TS 24.007, with EMM protocol discriminator, no EPS bearer identity, no procedure transaction identity, and IEs as listed in Table 8.2.26.1.**
